# Wish Upon a Star with the custom module modules/custom/lua/quest_workarounds.lua (no condition: on when listed), which
# replaces state 2's Enu onTrade: npcUtil.tradeHasExactly(trade, FALLEN_STAR), then 334 when the weather is NONE (any
# time) or SUNSHINE at night or midnight, else 337 (Lua's `a or b and c` is `a or (b and c)`). Accepted by GM with a
# Fallen Star. 12:00 (DAY) with SUNSHINE (`weather 1`): 337 (SUNSHINE but not night); the star with a Bone Chip: not
# exactly the star, nil; 20:00 (NIGHT) with CLOUDS (`weather 2`): 337 (night but neither NONE nor SUNSHINE); NIGHT with
# SUNSHINE: 334 (the quest's own would play 337), completed (four Bags of Cactus Stems, fame +50, the star taken).
# MIDNIGHT is #custom_midnight, NONE by day #custom_none. The zone's weather timer does not reroll the GM's weather
# here: no tick reaches its next roll (`wait` moves only the Vana'diel clock).
module modules/custom/lua/quest_workarounds.lua
lists BastokMarkets/Enu/onTrade BastokMarkets/onEventFinish/334
char zone=BastokMarkets pos=-253.7,-13,-92.3 lvl=30
quest Bastok.WishUponAStar accepted
item FallenStar
item BoneChip
login
weather 1                      # GM: SUNSHINE
trade Enu FallenStar x1        # 12:00, DAY, SUNSHINE: not night: 337
finish                         # 337 has no finish handler: the star kept
trade Enu FallenStar x1 BoneChip x1  # not exactly the star: nil
wait vana=8                    # 20:00: NIGHT
weather 2                      # GM: CLOUDS
trade Enu FallenStar x1        # NIGHT, CLOUDS: 337
finish
weather 1                      # GM: SUNSHINE
trade Enu FallenStar x1        # NIGHT, SUNSHINE: 334
finish                         # completed: four Bags of Cactus Stems, fame +50, the star taken
